  "text_pages": [
    "GACHON UNIVERSITY - Language Requirements\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nLanguage of Intuctions:\nKorean or English\nKorean Track\nStudents with TOPIK 3 or equivalent can take major/elective courses except for medical related courses in medical campus.\n(For master programs, TOPIK Level 4 or higher is required. )\nStudents take Korean language classess at the Korean language Center.\n→ Four subjects, three credits each, 12 credits in total for 10 weeks (Mon to Fri / 09:00 - 13:00 or 14:00 - 18:00)\nStudents without TOPIK 3 take Korean language classes at the liberal arts college.\n→ Five subjects, three credits each, 15 credits in total, three hours per day\nStudents can only take one basic elective courses about Korean or Korean culture.\nEnglish\nTrack\nOver TOEFL IBT 70 or IELTS 5.5 or TOEIC 700 score is required.\nStudents\ncan take English-taught major/elective courses except for medical related courses in medical campus.\nOnly Business and Computer Engineering majors are taught in English.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
